course: dictionary
lesson: 8461
title: Words for food
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are new because the thing they name is new to you. Context helps: read the words around the new word for clues. «kartOplya means potato, and kOvbasa is a salami-like sausage, while a hot-dog sausage is a sosyska.» The sentence compares the foods, so you can tell that a salami-like sausage is a sausage of its own kind, different from a hot-dog sausage.
explain: Salami is a large sausage made of dried, spiced meat, often pork. You eat it cold, in thin slices. Ask yourself what would fit in the sentence. A slice of salami fits on a pizza or in a sandwich, so you can guess it is a food you eat cold, not a drink or a toy.
explain: Salami is also a cured meat, which means it has been dried and preserved so it lasts a long time. Food safety notices use this word for that reason, so you may meet it on labels and in lists of foods.
fact: Salami is a large sausage made of dried, spiced meat, often pork.
fact: You eat salami cold, in thin slices.
fact: Salami is a common pizza topping and sandwich filling, and it comes from Italy.
fact: Salami is a cured meat, which means it is dried and preserved.
fact: In «kOvbasa is a salami-like sausage», the word salami-like tells you that kOvbasa is similar to salami.
exercise: What is salami? | *A large sausage of dried, spiced meat, eaten cold in thin slices | A hot drink served at breakfast | A kind of bread baked in an oven | A sweet fruit eaten with cream
exercise: «kartOplya means potato, and kOvbasa is a salami-like sausage, while a hot-dog sausage is a sosyska.» Which food is a salami-like sausage? | *kOvbasa | kartOplya | sosyska
exercise: Where would you most likely find salami slices? | In a glass of cold lemonade | *On a pizza or in a sandwich | On a bus timetable | In a pair of socks
test: In food safety, salami is described as what kind of meat? | A fresh fish | A cold drink | A sweet fruit | *A cured meat
test: Which phrase shows a common way to eat salami? | Salami fruit cake | Salami rain | *Salami pizza | Salami bicycle
exam: Mia reads «Pack the salami slices in the lunchbox.» What does salami mean? | A vegetable grown in gardens | A toy for the lunchbox | A cheese, soft and white | *A large sausage of dried, spiced meat, eaten cold
